WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:18.120
EPISODE I
COLOR TV

2
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.960
Brezhnev's dead!

3
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.400
What?
- He's dead!

4
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.920
Finally!

5
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.880
Pour me a shot!
- Are you sure?

6
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.320
Of course!
This calls for a toast.

7
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.400
If it's the wish of an
important party employee...

8
00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.000
I may work for the party,
but I'm still a human being.

9
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.560
Are you sure he's dead?
- The radio said so.

10
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.640
I doubt they joke with these matters.
Not that they do it anyway.

11
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.200
What do you mean, the radio?

12
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.400
Yes, the radio.

13
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.800
Listen,
they're playing funeral music.

14
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.040
Why should they announce
our neighbor's death?

15
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.320
Is he dead?
- You said so!

16
00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.040
No, I didn't!
- You came in and said Kessner's dead!

17
00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.080
I didn't say that!
- I heard you!

18
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.680
Hell, you heard wrong!
- If you didn't say Kessner,

19
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.960
then what did you say?
- Brezhnev.

20
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.880
What about him?
- He's dead.

21
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.520
What?
Can't be.

22
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.640
He's dead?
Are you absolutely sure?

23
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.320
Oh, come on, dear.
What's wrong?

24
00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.760
I didn't realize his death
would upset you so much.

25
00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.920
Go to hell!
What do I care about Brezhnev!

26
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.560
I've always hoped that eventually
we'll live here by ourselves.

27
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.800
Then you came in and said that.
- I never said...

28
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.080
Yes, you did!
But who cares now!

29
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.680
I don't want to share the kitchen
and the toilet any more!

30
00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.920
You always get my hopes up!
- I never got anything up.

31
00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.840
Don't worry,
Kessner's time will come too.

32
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.160
Did you say that Brezhnev's dead?

33
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.760
Didn't you hear me earlier?

34
00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:11.160
I have to go to work, now!

35
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.520
Isn't this your day off?
- Yes, but they might need me.

36
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.280
There's probably lots of people
who can arrange the funeral.

37
00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.800
I'll deny that Vokk-woman the
satisfaction to nag at me later on:

38
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.200
"Where were you, at such a tragic
moment for our country?"

39
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.040
Dear lord,
I can't leave looking like this!

40
00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.240
Don't worry,
you look perfect for today.

41
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.760
Leonid Ilyich Brezhnev,
the General Secretary of the CPSU

42
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.120
and a long- term leader of the country.

43
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.840
Gave himself four
Hero of Soviet Union awards.

44
00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.520
Declared himself a writer.

45
00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.520
Was a living corpse
for the final years of his life.

46
00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.240
It was a public secret

47
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.560
that his date of death was simply
the day they pulled the plug.

48
00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.800
Currently, as the
imperialistic aggressors

49
00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.640
are trying to bring about
a nuclear disaster,

50
00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.680
we can clearly feel Leonid Ilyich's
effort towards peace.

51
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:16.920
He understood the role young people
play in the fight for peace

52
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.440
and towards a better future.
His speeches, books...

53
00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.800
Now what?

54
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.680
Nothing. They'll pick one even older.
- No one's older than Brezhnev.

55
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.720
Have you seen the podium
during parades?

56
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.280
It's a line of fossils,
they don't have young people.

57
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.600
They should pick someone
who's at least able to speak.

58
00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.240
Or senile enough to open
Finnish border.

59
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.640
You wish!

60
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.720
Finland is already
Russia's appendage.

61
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.720
I simply want to go buy
records and jeans there.

62
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.560
If that really was the case,

63
00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.520
you'd soon find that the records
are the same as here,

64
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.040
and jeans look a lot
like Sangar clothes.

65
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.480
Son of...
Have you heard?

66
00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.080
What, did they open the border?
- Brezhnev's dead.

67
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.120
But you already knew.

68
00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.040
Yeah!
Propeller's un-banned again.

69
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.400
Turn it off.
The neighbors!

70
00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.560
That geront's death changes nothing.

71
00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:51.080
The party's cafeteria will still sell
smoked sausage and clementines.

72
00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.040
Perhaps we should...

73
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.480
Võsa speaking.

74
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.760
Yes, of course.

75
00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.680
I understand.

76
00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.920
My deepest condolences to you, too.

77
00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.840
Yes, I understand.

78
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.240
Thank you.
- Well?

79
00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:28.440
Entertainment business
will be closed for three days.

80
00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.080
Damn!

81
00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.840
What's the matter?
Don't you like free days?

82
00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.880
No!
I mean, yes!

83
00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:42.880
My birthday's day after tomorrow.
I had tickets to Viru Variety.

84
00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:46.960
Forget it!
Celebrate at home.

85
00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:53.640
The chef of Viru culinary.
Order what you need.

86
00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.600
Don't invite me,
I'll be off hunting.

87
00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.680
Comrade Võsa,
thank you so much!

88
00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:09.720
Viru culinary,
a legendary business in Tallinn

89
00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:14.360
that filled pre- orders for scarce
semi-fabricated foods.

90
00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.360
If stores sold eggs,
Viru provided deviled eggs.

91
00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.320
If stores were out of minced meat,
Viru sold at least meatloaf.

92
00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.880
Rumor went that the dishes
were made out of food

93
00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.160
left over from the Finns
staying in Viru hotel.

94
00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:39.640
Kadak speaking!
Yes, how to put this...

95
00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.440
Yes, yes we are.

96
00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:51.960
I see, very well.

97
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:57.360
Have a nice day.
- What did Vokk want?

98
00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:02.040
Asked whether
we're are feeling mournful.

99
00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.920
Said she's sick
and will stay at home today.

100
00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:08.880
I know what's wrong with her.

101
00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.320
She went to Narva yesterday,
to open a production line,

102
00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.760
and ate bad lamprey.

103
00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.840
But I never told you that.
- And I never heard.

104
00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.920
Congratulations, boy!

105
00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.880
Your daughter's birthday's coming up.
- I know!

106
00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.840
I celebrate Brezhnev's
descent to hell.

107
00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.360
I hope he rots there,
may God torment his soul.

108
00:08:54.760 --> 00:09:00.200
Hopefully they won't embalm him,
so he'll rot with all of his awards.

109
00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.600
Aadu, the neighbors!
- I don't care about our red neighbors.

110
00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:12.880
But you know, don't call me Aadu!
- Okay, Aadu, what shall I call you?

111
00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.280
Just call me pop.

112
00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.520
You've been living
with my daughter for five years,

113
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:26.280
won her over from that damned sailor.
And good for you!

114
00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.200
Been together for five years...

115
00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:36.680
Wait, what was I saying?
Ah yes, pop sounds right.

116
00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.360
Okay, pop!
- One more okay,

117
00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:44.760
and I'll be mister to you!
Fore- and surname included!

118
00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.000
Okay... okay. Okay?
- Okay's okay.

119
00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.720
A drink, pop?

120
00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.600
Only Estonian vodka,
I never drink Russian stuff.

121
00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.600
Son of a ...!

122
00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.800
Did you steal again?

123
00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:07.280
From the Russian state, always!
Its a matter of principle.

124
00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.040
Is your Mustamäe garage full of them?
- Yes, to the brim.

125
00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:14.640
Next summer we'll build a garage.

126
00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.400
You don't even own a car.
- That's not my fault.

127
00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:24.000
If Estonian SR built cars,
I would have all the parts by now.

128
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.000
You can call me Ats,
from time to time.

129
00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:30.880
Okay, boy,
I'll try to remember that.

130
00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.400
The Voice of America will be on soon!

131
00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:40.080
I wonder what they say
about this grand event.

132
00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.240
But we haven't toasted yet!
- Later, later!

133
00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.520
But why?

134
00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.840
The country's mourning.
We can't have a party.

135
00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:11.000
Võsa told me to celebrate at home.
Even gave me Viru chef's number.

136
00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.880
But who'll find out?
We'll keep to ourselves.

137
00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:22.240
Pull the curtains, like Christmas.

138
00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.560
What about the neighbors?

139
00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.600
To hell with them.
Old Nikifor is almost dead,

140
00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:30.480
and we haven't seen
his old hag for days.

141
00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:34.040
And the militsiya-guy?
- Whom do you mean?

142
00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.960
He's an idiot,
he'll be oblivious.

143
00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:46.080
Know what? It seems to me
that they all died a while ago.

144
00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.080
I'm not joking.

145
00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.840
I heard the hag use the toilet
this morning.

146
00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.920
Oh, missis Kessner!

147
00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:45.200
Missis? A bourgeois title!

148
00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.720
I didn't meant to insult you...

149
00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.280
Stop babbling!

150
00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:54.600
You can call me missis at home.
What do you want?

151
00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:59.600
I came to invite you
to the communal kitchen.

152
00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:02.080
We're having a small sit-together.
- Yes, and?

153
00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.720
To commemorate the great man.
- Who?

154
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.800
Leonid Ilyich, of course.

155
00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.800
He was a good man indeed.

156
00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.800
So, perhaps you
and your husband can join us?

157
00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:17.960
No, unfortunately Nikifor is very ill.
I can't leave him alone.

158
00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.720
And I can't haul him in on my back,
that would be improper.

159
00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.760
Yes, improper.

160
00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:27.680
But how's he doing?
I heard that he's been better lately.

161
00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.280
No, he won't recover from this.

162
00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.240
It's more probable that stores
will start selling bananas.

163
00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.440
I'm very sorry that you can't join us.

164
00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:42.200
We kept two seats for you,
but we understand, naturally.

165
00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:44.440
It's my duty to stay here.

166
00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.680
But thank you, boy,
for the invite.

167
00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.200
Viru culinary!
- Hello, I'd like to make an order.

168
00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.000
How soon?
- For tomorrow.

169
00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.520
Impossible!
- What do you mean, impossible?

170
00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.160
It's not New Year's eve,
or Women's Day.

171
00:14:18.280 --> 00:14:22.720
Listen, I would like to order...
- We don't have time to fill it!

172
00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.360
You're not the only one
who wants to celebrate.

173
00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.800
You can't possibly have
a queue right now.

174
00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:31.160
Listen, I have a birthday...
oh, I see.

175
00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:38.360
Please, get a pen and paper, and
write down exactly what I tell you.

176
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:43.800
Didn't you hear what I just said?
- No, you didn't hear me!

177
00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:47.720
I'm calling from the central committee
of the communist party.

178
00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:51.880
My name is Sirje Kadak. I'd like to
order some culinary products

179
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:58.720
for Leonid Ilyich's funeral feast.
- Yes, comrade Kadak, one moment!

180
00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.560
And some other items.

181
00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.480
First, the drinks.

182
00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:15.760
Two bottles of Belõi Aist,
four Sovetskoje Polusladkoje...

183
00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.240
On this sad hour, we promise
to never stray from the path

184
00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:40.440
laid out by the party.
Each and every one of us

185
00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:44.760
shall make an even bigger effort,
and respond to our loss

186
00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:49.240
by achieving new feats of labour.
We shall use our strength

187
00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:54.760
and knowledge to carry out
the decisions of the 26. congress.

188
00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:32.640
Happy birthday, darling!
- Thank you, dear!

189
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:38.000
Is mine the first?
- No, the children gave theirs already.

190
00:16:38.360 --> 00:16:39.760
What did they get you?

191
00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.080
Pille gave hand made oven mittens,
like she has before,

192
00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:50.320
but Alex and Paavo got me this!

193
00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:58.000
That's Finnish, right?
- Yes, and look at the colors!

194
00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.080
Look at you!

195
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.240
For this I can forgive Paavo,

196
00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:08.440
that he's risking his future
over there at Viru.

197
00:17:08.680 --> 00:17:11.880
Look at my gift too!
- Lets see, lets see.

198
00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:34.400
Oh my goodness!
A mixer, how sweet.

199
00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:37.160
The old Russian one broke down.
Do you like it?

200
00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:42.320
DDR! Oh, my darling!
Where did you get it?

201
00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.440
Does it really matter?

202
00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.880
Not important at all!

203
00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:55.040
Tonight we'll make
ice cream cocktails, German style.

204
00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:16.080
Hello!

205
00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:22.440
Villem, how did you get here?
- A wave cast me ashore!

206
00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:28.120
What are you ogling at, landlubber,
come give me a hand!

207
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.000
Let's lift it somewhere.
- Ats, come help the master!

208
00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.120
What's this?
- What do you think it is?

209
00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.480
Let's put it here!

210
00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:45.000
Is that really a color TV?

211
00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:50.640
Color television set.
Every Estonian's dream.

212
00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:54.040
Weren't available in stores.
Could only be bought

213
00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:57.360
with union's purchase permission,
or via contacts.

214
00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:02.160
Old color TVs were huge wooden boxes,
that even two men could barely lift.

215
00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:09.200
Yes, this is a color TV indeed.
Satko!

216
00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:16.440
Shows colors from red to pink.
It shows everything.

217
00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.400
Why did you bring it here?

218
00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.960
Did you think I'd forget the
50th anniversary of my official wife?

219
00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:28.800
No, Villem is not that kind of a guy.

220
00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:34.920
This is for you, a gift!
Come here, happy birthday.

221
00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:45.040
A new make-up set!
Not bad, not bad.

222
00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:49.920
All the whores in Rotterdam
paint their faces the same way.

223
00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.280
They live a wonderful life,

224
00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.920
have opportunities
our women can't even dream of.

225
00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:03.840
Lets make one thing very clear.
First of all, I'm 45,

226
00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:08.480
and secondly,
the TV is too expensive.

227
00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.440
Well, you'll be 50 soon!

228
00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:17.680
Besides, Villem can give his wife
gifts for her 45th birthday, too.

229
00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:23.840
But if you don't want it,
I'll take it to the neighbors' place.

230
00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:29.240
I bet old Nikifor would love to watch
Vremja in color on his deathbed.

231
00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.080
No, no, leave it there.

232
00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:36.440
What's this? Someone else's gift?

233
00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:40.920
A mixer?
- That's a very useful gadget.

234
00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:43.280
But of course, of course.

235
00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:49.920
The sad news is, though,
that I have to get back on the ship.

236
00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:54.960
No time to celebrate with you.
- So, you're not staying?

237
00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:58.680
No, unfortunately not.
You'll be on your own.

238
00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:03.000
Oh right, Ats, keep
an eye on my wife, okay?

239
00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:06.200
Keep her from straying, right?

240
00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.640
When will you return?

241
00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:11.760
I don't know. But I'll be back
sooner than before.

242
00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:15.200
I'm less homesick now,
because I know

243
00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:19.360
that when you watch the TV,
you'll think of me.

244
00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:21.200
<i>Ciao! Arrivederci!</i>

245
00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.040
That guy!
- Relax!

246
00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:30.400
Shit! I'm not going to watch
a single thing on that TV!

247
00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.680
I almost forgot!

248
00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:36.640
Here's some records
and other stuff for the kids.

249
00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:40.200
Tell them daddy said hi!
Ciao!

250
00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.280
Do you know this one?

251
00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:59.400
Estonian, Russian and German
are on the same plane,

252
00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:02.400
and the German throws out
a pack of cigarettes, exclaiming:

253
00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.360
"We have plenty of those!"

254
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.880
The Russian throws out
a bottle of vodka and...

255
00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.200
Why won't they turn on the TV?

256
00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:15.280
So, the Russian throws out
a bottle of vodka and says:

257
00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:17.280
"We have plenty of those!"

258
00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.080
Estonian throws out the...

259
00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:21.600
Wait, wait, listen!

260
00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:25.680
Estonian throws out the Russian
and says: "We have plenty of those!"

261
00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:31.720
Let's switch on the TV!
We can watch Finnish channels.

262
00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:37.200
TV's without the color unit.
We need someone to install it.

263
00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:39.880
One man is able to get his hands on
a color TV,

264
00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:42.000
the other one can't even get
a color unit.

265
00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:43.680
Paavo!
- They have waiting lines.

266
00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.160
Why can't we watch the old
black and white one?

267
00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:49.600
Because it's being repaired
and it's black and white.

268
00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:54.080
We really only need a bit more blue.

269
00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:59.000
What? What?

270
00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:06.520
What about Estonian
or Leningrad television?

271
00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:08.800
No, they only broadcast funeral music.

272
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:14.360
If my wife doesn't want to
listen that on her birthday,

273
00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:16.320
it's her right!

274
00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:19.520
She's as much your wife
as Brezhnev was your dad.

275
00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:20.880
Paavo!
- Stop it!

276
00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:26.120
It's my daughter's birthday today,
so no arguing!

277
00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:29.360
Paavo, go pick us some good music.

278
00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:34.360
And afterwards we'll watch TV.

279
00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:37.600
I want to see Vremja tonight!

280
00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:47.360
I want to hear what that new guy,
Antropov, has to say.

281
00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:53.360
Now excuse me, I have to go to
where even the General Secretaries

282
00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:54.880
go by themselves.

283
00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:59.160
Pille's there!
- I'll wait!

284
00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:14.040
Ats!

285
00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.960
Dance with me!

286
00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:27.040
Happy birthday!

287
00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:43.000
Quiet!

288
00:24:46.680 --> 00:24:50.080
Aino said that she and her son
accept our invitation

289
00:24:50.280 --> 00:24:54.560
and will join the funeral dinner.
Apparently, Nikifor fell asleep.

290
00:24:54.720 --> 00:24:57.440
What invitation?
- What funeral dinner?

291
00:24:58.760 --> 00:25:02.160
No time to explain!
Now we act!

292
00:25:05.920 --> 00:25:10.240
And now, dear friends, I'm going
to ask Ats' girlfriend for dance!

293
00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:23.720
Comrade Kadak, it seems to me

294
00:25:23.840 --> 00:25:26.760
that your father is not
in a very grieving mood.

295
00:25:27.200 --> 00:25:30.840
Oh, no, he has these episodes
when tragic things happen.

296
00:25:31.480 --> 00:25:33.920
Yes, yes, it's true.

297
00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:37.720
Are we going to dance tonight?

298
00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:39.880
No, no.

299
00:25:42.360 --> 00:25:48.240
No! I said stance, not dance!
I work in a factory, right?

300
00:25:49.120 --> 00:25:52.200
I thought I'd make some
small memorial medals,

301
00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:55.480
and show her correct stance,
how to make them, you know.

302
00:25:55.840 --> 00:25:58.840
I thought ask
my daughter to help me.

303
00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:03.280
Invite you daughter
to a secret factory?

304
00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:06.120
That's prohibited!
- You are correct,

305
00:26:06.440 --> 00:26:08.640
and we won't speak of it again.

306
00:26:15.440 --> 00:26:18.680
A toast! To good health,
I mean his memory!

307
00:26:35.720 --> 00:26:39.560
Too bad that we can't see
Finnish broadcast of the funeral.

308
00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:42.720
What does it matter?
Funeral's a funeral.

309
00:26:43.960 --> 00:26:49.880
Would have heard their comments.
- The Finns say nothing.

310
00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:54.600
Their mouths are full of Russian di..
- Father! We have guests!

311
00:27:00.400 --> 00:27:02.920
This TV's image quality is superb.

312
00:27:05.680 --> 00:27:08.360
Yes, Brezhnev's
never been more beautiful.

313
00:27:10.440 --> 00:27:13.960
They left out the part where
he fell into the hole!

314
00:27:14.200 --> 00:27:15.920
Father!
- But they did!

315
00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:19.600
I knew it.
